 @tomp6319 it was worth it for me. I solely play warzone though. Decided to keep the 9060 xt after playing for about 6 hours and feeling a more enjoyable experience.

My advice - which I’d take for a grain of salt - if you can get one and your trade in value is similar to mine just go for it. 

Use the card and if it’s an upgraded experience keep it then send your old card in to complete the trade. If not return the Amd and keep your old card. Like test driving a car

 @Lennox032  Its raw bandwidth... the bit bus has nothing to do with texture pop.

128 bit is simply 4 x 32 bit controller layout on die. 192 bit is 6 x 32 bit, and 256 is 8 x 32 bit.

The bandwidth on a 5060TI is the same as 3070 from 2 generations ago.  These will perform the same in game in regards to texture pop, regardless of bit bus.

